  "term": "automatism defense",
  "definition": "An automatism defense is a courtroom claim that a person committed an act while in a blackout or automatic state rather than under conscious control. In this packet, it is discussed specifically as a non-insane automatism defense, with culture sometimes offered as an explanation for what led to the blackout.",
